Every consumer of the from-source mbedtls compiles against ITS headers and ITS config
(splanc #468).

Two halves, one invariant ("a TU that includes <mbedtls/*.h> sees exactly the struct
layouts of the mbedtls the image links"):

1. nix/mbedtls_src.BUILD: MBEDTLS_CONFIG_FILE (and the c3 variant's
   LM_MBEDTLS_NO_HW_ECC) move from copts to `defines`, so they propagate to every
   dependent. Before, only mbedtls_src's own sources had the -D; a consumer that did not
   repeat it by hand got upstream's default mbedtls/mbedtls_config.h, a different config:
   splanc's netstack transport compiled a 344 B mbedtls_ssl_context (library: 552 B) and a
   224 B mbedtls_ssl_config (library: 196 B), and mbedtls_ssl_init overran its g_ssl by
   208 B. (The prebuilt SDK's flags/defines carries -DMBEDTLS_CONFIG_FILE=
   "mbedtls/esp_config.h", but :sdk_hdrs does not.) CONFIG_MBEDTLS_DYNAMIC_BUFFER stays a
   private copt: only port/dynamic/*.c read it, no header does.

2. nix/arduino_esp32.BUILD: drop the prebuilt SDK's mbedtls include dirs from :sdk_hdrs
   (esp32c6 + esp32c3; the classic esp32 section still links the prebuilt mbedtls and is
   untouched). They preceded @mbedtls_src's on every consumer's include path. The headers
   are byte-identical today (both mbedtls 3.6.5 / IDF v5.5.4), so this changes no layout,
   but it makes @mbedtls_src's the ONLY mbedtls headers a TU can reach: one that includes
   them without depending on @mbedtls_src (and so without its config) now fails to
   compile instead of silently mismatching. esp_crt_bundle/include stays (not mbedtls).

Applied after the other mbedtls patches; fold upstream on the next embedded bump.

